          "name": "pdf123_run_tool",
          "canonical_hash": "sha256:4af9d7585f0c9252e98bc5f8d28ad535762cc6364cccd78ec8fa05ff4d87bbc6",
          "description": "Run one PDF123 tool on local files. The files are uploaded to the PDF123 API (or PDFX_API_BASE), processed, and deleted there; the result is saved locally and its path returned. JSON reports (e.g. get-info) are returned inline. Several files with a single-file tool (compress, rotate, protect, convert, ...) run as a batch: one result per file, saved as each finishes, and one file failing does not stop the others (a batch with any failure comes back as an error with the per-file report attached). A batch of a JSON-report tool returns the reports inline, keyed by input, and writes files only when output is given. Filter tools (filter-*) answer {\\",
